{"seq":15,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T14:21:12.839Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0be54efa187191940cbe80d5f84e62105f248449eefdf5d647682228cb0e99fb","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes. Two of them have Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n1. #4419: gatehouse barcode scanners not reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md).\n\n2. #PD-4492: Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at the Eau Claire yard, Doors 14-18, weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk on the 04:00 shift. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through fine. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\", 5 Oct 2025 (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md).\n\nThe other Moss notes have no QFL ticket numbers. That's the 14 Sep 2025 North pipeline digest, the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in and the two Central notes. The tickets in the Central notes (#4409, #4412, FR-882) are for Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n\nTwo other things:\n- The cheat sheet warns not to mix QFL up with Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\"), which isn't a customer.\n- Your own 9 Apr 2026 renewal debrief notes also mention ticket #8841 (carrier portal timeout on CSV manifests over 600 rows). That one isn't from Moss, so leave it out if the weekly note should only cover Moss's sources."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
